 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "pev2IbbzCgAJ",
   "from": "Mike",
   "author": "175e6319aab23650",
   "date": "2017-04-10T16:29:41Z",
   "subject": "geom_point isn't using data from my dataframe",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have a matrix that I converted to a dataframe using as.data.frame, it has several rows and columns and has column and row names.<br><br>When I plot like this it works:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dataframe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dataframe$</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;X&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dataframe$</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>When I plot like this I get a single point:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dataframe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;X&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Y&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>It seems that using the second method the actual data in the specified X and Y columns isn&#39;t being used and instead it&#39;s treating &quot;X&quot; and &quot;Y&quot; as factors hence the single data point. How can I fix this, Is there a problem with how my dataframe is formatted?<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sQaXuoL3CgAJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2017-04-10T17:39:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: geom_point isn't using data from my dataframe",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Mike, <div><br></div><div>ggplot uses non-standard evaluation so when you are giving it variables you don&#39;t quote them. </div><div>When you give it this:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggplot</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dataframe</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> aes</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;X&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Y&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Likely when you are plotting aes(&quot;X&quot;, &quot;Y&quot;) it is literally plotting the factor X by factor Y and that would be a single point. It is ignoring your dataframe entirely. <br></div><div><br></div><div>This should work as intended:</div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggplot</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dataframe</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> aes</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,136,0)\">X</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><font color=\"#008800\">Y</font></span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you want to quote them (for programming reasons) use aes_string()</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggplot</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dataframe</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> aes_string</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;X&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Y&quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;font-size:10.4px;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><br></div><div>ggplot(mtcars, aes_string(&quot;cyl&quot;, &quot;mpg&quot;)) + geom_point() # this works<br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>B</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
