  {
   "id": "TniLIUr7CgAJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2017-04-10T18:48:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: geom_point isn't using data from my dataframe",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Mike, <div><br></div><div>Symbols in column names usually cause trouble. In dplyr stuff I often see backticks help ` `. </div><div><br></div><div>You can plot using them and &quot;NSE&quot; as follows:</div><div>ggplot(mtcars, aes(`cyl`, `mpg`)) + geom_point()<br></div><div><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>B</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Apr 10, 2017 at 11:41 AM, Mike <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lev...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thank you for the reply. I was using quotes because my column headings aren&#39;t actually X and Y (I probably should have given the actual names) they are strings with special characters (+ and - symbols) in them) but even with aes_string and quoting the values they don&#39;t work (object not found). Once I changed the names to simpler text they work as expected so I will change the names for now.<br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
